   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the town of\nPoughkeepsie to impose a hotel and motel tax; and providing for the repeal of\nsuch provisions upon expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S9025",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9025-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1202-nnn, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9025\n\nSPONSOR: ROLISON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the town of\nPoughkeepsie to impose a hotel and motel tax; and providing for the\nrepeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to authorize the Town of Poughkeepsie to\nestablish a hotel and motel occupancy tax.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new section 1202-nnn to the Tax Law, which will author-\nize and empower the Town of Poughkeepsie, located in Dutchess County, to\nadopt and amend local laws imposing a tax of up to 5% upon persons occu-\npying hotel or motel rooms in such town.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAt the request of the municipality, this legislation would allow the\nTown of Poughkeepsie, located in Dutchess County, to impose a hotel and\nmotel tax. The rate of such tax shall not exceed 5% of the daily rental\nrate for each room. This shall include facilities commonly known as \"bed\nand breakfast\" and \"tourist\" facilities, such as an Airbnb. Pursuant to\nthe Municipal Home Rule Law, a town may adopt local laws that relate to\nthe levy and administration of local taxes if authorized by the State\nlegislature. This tax would enable the town to raise additional revenue,\nallowing them to continue to provide necessary services without having\nto increase property tax rates.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:;\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the State. The town will collect additional revenues.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed 3 years after such date.\n",
